      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I wasn't familiar with those tools, but a brief glance seems to indicate that they export their animation files as JSON, which is promising. Udon has a built in JSON parser here: https://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/udon/data-containers/vrcjson/. Using this, I bet that it would be possible to adapt their runtime package or build your own to support their format. This would probably require a decent amount of knowledge on Udon and programming, though.\n\nUnfortunately it is exceedingly rare for VRChat to include an external package these days, so some amount of getting it working yourself is probably your best bet.\n\nYou could also wait until Udon 2, which will support the full C# specification, as opposed to current Udon which is just a small subset. If their package makes use of complex features that are not available in Udon currently, it might be better to just wait for Udon 2, where the conversion should be much simpler.",
